    {
      "id": "UgwTMmM60OW7Ebm5QTt4AaABAg",
      "author": "@porschedriverful",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mPAwk4cGZ_3fF1sOX1ZLzMLT65-N0BPsVEcbOT0p7st6A=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Some Honourable mentions that you could visit up North are the Frisian lakes, Zwolle, The province of Drenthe if you love cycling especially around Dwingeloo and Diever area. Close to Rotterdam its worth it to go down towards Zeeland and experience the delta works. This is the water defense system that keep most of the Netherlands safe. And it lovely to experience at Neeltje Jans. We have two great attraction parks Walibi and the theme park De Efteling. If you love parks like Disney Land but would love to have it themed around fairy tales then this is the experience for you. While in the Netherlands try to enjoy our water sports and if you are with a big group you can even rent massive sailboat experiences in for example the Frisian lakes. Visit the many art museums that feature famous Dutch artists. If anyone else has some great suggestions comment them below.",
      "likeCount": 1,
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-25T19:09:41Z",
      "replyCount": 1,
